From 5fd76cbd7ddd38abfa9ba08d6a804591ddab101e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?No=C3=A9=20Lopez?= <noelopez@free.fr>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 23:23:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Notify gnome-session when startup is done.

This is needed to wait for mutter to have set its environment variables before
having gnome-session-shepherd start the other services.

We simply replace systemd-notify with gherd’s notification mechanism.

See also (gnome-session-shepherd)Notifications.

Upstream-Status: Not applicable.
---
 src/shell-util.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/shell-util.c b/src/shell-util.c
index a965c7148..52b030cc8 100644
--- a/src/shell-util.c
+++ b/src/shell-util.c
@@ -772,9 +772,10 @@ shell_util_systemd_unit_exists_finish (GAsyncResult  *res,
 void
 shell_util_sd_notify (void)
 {
-  /* We only use NOTIFY_SOCKET exactly once; unset it so it doesn't remain in
-   * our environment. */
-  sd_notify (1, "READY=1");
+  if (-1 == system ("gherd notify gnome-session-meta org.gnome.Shell"))
+  {
+    g_warning ("Failed to notify gnome-session.");
+  }
 }
 
